The barista smiles at me.
I hold my card over the terminal.
The machine beeps.
"Do you want a receipt?" he asks.
"No thank you," I answer.
I walk over to the wall.
I take my thick winter coat from a hook.
I put the coat on.
I also put my scarf on.
Now I am ready for the cold.
I look at the barista again.
"Thank you very much for the coffee," I say.
"You are welcome," he says with a smile.
"Have a good day."
"Likewise," I say.
I walk over to the front door.
I push the heavy door open.
The wind is cold, but I feel good.
